00:02:48.619 --> 00:02:53.207
I will get "Neha" as output because in the 'Dictionary'
"Neha" is corresponding to " 567 "

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:55.633
This is how we can work with 'Dictionaries'

00:02:55.658 --> 00:02:56.417
Now look,

00:02:56.561 --> 00:02:58.834
Dictionaries are ordered collection
of data items.

00:02:58.875 --> 00:03:01.381
They store multiple items in
a single variable.

00:03:01.582 --> 00:03:08.483
Dictionary items are key-value pairs that are separated
by commas and enclosed within curly brackets

00:03:08.522 --> 00:03:14.302
What happens is, Python 3.7 onwards
'Dictionaries' are ordered collection

00:03:14.337 --> 00:03:16.604
Earlier dictionaries used to be unordered

00:03:16.865 --> 00:03:22.616
You have to keep this mind, your 'Dict' is ordered or
unordered depends on which Python version you're using

00:03:22.972 --> 00:03:24.612
What does Ordered &amp; Unordered mean?

00:03:24.637 --> 00:03:28.979
It means whenever I'll print it's keys
I'll get them in same order

00:03:29.207 --> 00:03:31.830
How can we print keys?
I'll tell you

